   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the building inspector in the town of Wilson, county of Niagara,\nto reside outside such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S7053",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7053-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7053\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the building inspector in the town of Wilson, county of\nNiagara, to reside outside such town\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Town of Wilson building inspector to\nreside outside the town.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Town Law to allow the Wilson Town building inspec-\ntor to not be an elector of the Town.\n\nSection 2 amends the public officers law to remove the requirement that\nthe Town of Wilson building inspector be a resident of the Town.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is at the request of the Town of Wilson. In recent\nyears the Town has had continued difficulties in recruiting and retain-\ning individuals to serve as their building inspector. Prior Towns have\nfaced similar concerns and have secured exemptions from this law.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
